:- module(prlm_plan,
          [ plan_spec/3,
            req_ops/2,
            plan_append/3,
            number_ops/3
          ]).

/** <module> prlm_plan — in-language RLM plan construction (stage1 material)

This is language, not library: ordinary Prolog text executed by the stage0
kernel machine (prolog/prlm_kernel.pl), loaded into the session engine by
prolog/prlm_rlm.pl and reached there through module `prlm_rlm_lang`
(which imports this module's exports; a local clause in `prlm_rlm_lang`
shadows this one, which is how plans are specialised in-language).

Contract (shapes shared with the host dispatcher in prolog/prlm_rlm.pl)
=======================================================================

    plan_spec(spec(SpecId, Goal, Mode, Reqs), Tools, Steps)

  * SpecId : atom.  Goal : ground term.
  * Mode   : the RESOLVED mode (direct|symbolic|symbolic_recursive), not the
    requested one.
  * Reqs   : [req(Id, Desc, Check), ...] in spec order.
  * Tools  : list of tool-name atoms (host side: names of prlm_tool_discover,
    already deterministically ordered by name).
  * Steps  : [step(n(I), Op), ...] with I = 1,2,3,... in plan order.
    The step id is the compound n(I): the stage0 engine has no atom
    construction, so positional ids are structured terms.  The host
    dispatcher uses the identical shape, so plans are host/lang comparable.

Op shapes understood by the host dispatcher:

  * tool_call_step(FirstTool, none) — PREPENDED exactly when Mode == symbolic
    and Tools \= [].  Documented approximation of NeedsTools: resolved
    symbolic is what NeedsTools=true yields, and this predicate sees only the
    resolved mode.  Args `none` means "no arguments"; the host dispatcher
    converts it to the empty args dict at the tool gate.
  * verify_step(ReqId) — one per requirement, in Reqs order.
  * yield_step(goal_done(Goal)) — always the FINAL step.

The whole plan is deterministic and total: exactly one solution for any
ground input.  Implementation uses only the stage0 builtin surface (list
recursion, arithmetic, if-then-else); the engine exposes no append/member,
hence the local helpers below.
*/

plan_spec(spec(_SpecId, Goal, Mode, Reqs), Tools, Steps) :-
    (   Mode == symbolic,
        Tools = [FirstTool|_]
    ->  Pre = [tool_call_step(FirstTool, none)]
    ;   Pre = []
    ),
    req_ops(Reqs, VerifyOps),
    plan_append(Pre, VerifyOps, Mid),
    plan_append(Mid, [yield_step(goal_done(Goal))], Ops),
    number_ops(Ops, 1, Steps).

req_ops([], []).
req_ops([req(Id, _, _)|Reqs], [verify_step(Id)|Ops]) :-
    req_ops(Reqs, Ops).

plan_append([], L, L).
plan_append([X|Xs], L, [X|R]) :-
    plan_append(Xs, L, R).

number_ops([], _, []).
number_ops([Op|Ops], N, [step(n(N), Op)|Steps]) :-
    N1 is N + 1,
    number_ops(Ops, N1, Steps).
